  <issue>
  File explorer enhancements
# Description

I have some suggestions on how to enhance the spyder file explorer panel:

At the moment if a file-type/content is supported by the spyder editor, it has an context action "Edit", otherwise it has the somewhat ubiquitous entry "Open" which delegates to the OS. This also results in folders having an "Open" command that opens the OS file explorer at that position.

I came up with these ideas, after trying to delete multiple files at once from within spyder. Which apparently is not possible because a) there is no multiselection+delete b) I could not easily switch to the OS file explorer and delete them there.
# Todo

I would propose
- [ ] an dedicated context menu entry for "open in OS file explorer" common to both files and folders.
- [ ] a "open via OS" action, i.e. allow the OS to determine what program to use to open the file.
- [ ] remove "Open" on folders ~~(or change its function to actually opening it in the spyder file 
  explorer, i.e. same as double-click action)~~
- [ ] Add multiselection (i.e. Ctrl/Shift+Click) and enable the (appropriate?) context menu actions to work on that selection. 
- [ ] remove "global" options from context menu. Move them to panel options menu instead.
  </issue>
  
